    "diagnosis": "Hydroa vacciniforme lymphoproliferative disorder",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "At low magnification, the lymphoid infiltrate is centred in the dermis, showing a superficial and deep perivascular pattern involving the subcutaneous fat, with associated epidermal necrosis (&lt;&lt;31375&gt;&gt;). The lymphoid infiltrate is composed of a dense population of atypical lymphocytes of intermediate size (&lt;&lt;31376&gt;&gt;). The atypical cells are positive for EBV, as demonstrated by EBV-encoded small RNA (EBER) in&nbsp;situ hybridization (&lt;&lt;38994&gt;&gt;).",
